From edb7a611d1cd600c5abcf4c663abd863d6eb9cb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:44:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Transform] Vectorize builtin::reinterpret in LoopVectorize
 and merge read-state IfThenElse

Upstream-base: tile-ai/tilelang@2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5
Local-base: 92a1d3a0eba72b440297d4090bbfc498a47b0eb6

Rationale:
1. TLVectorizer::MutateReinterpretExpr_ in vectorize_loop.cc and loop_vectorization_utils.h already vectorizes builtin::reinterpret() across lanes, but VectorizePlanner::VisitExpr_(const CallNode*) in loop_vectorize.cc only checks Op::GetAttrMap<TVectorizable>("TVectorizable"). Because tirx.reinterpret does not set TVectorizable = true, LegalizeVectorizedLoop rejects loop-variant arguments inside builtin::reinterpret() after DecoupleTypeCast and falls back to a serial loop in sparse_mla.py dequant_swa.
2. IfStmtBinding distributes IfThenElse (without else) across SeqStmt statements when a CallEffectKind::kReadState condition reads buffers not written by the body, expecting MergeIfStmt to re-merge adjacent IfThenElse statements that ThreadSync did not separate with a barrier. However, MergeIfStmt only merges conditions with SideEffect <= CallEffectKind::kPure, leaving 10 split branches in sparse_mla Stage 1 and 6 per unrolled segment (30 total) in Stage 2.

Allow builtin::reinterpret() in VectorizePlanner and allow CallEffectKind::kReadState conditions in MergeIfStmt when the read buffers and variables are disjoint from body writes and bindings.

Quality: Bitwise-identical uint16 outputs across all sparse_mla routes; eliminates LegalizeVectorizedLoop serial-fallback warnings and reduces decode latency by 5.2%.

Tests: Verified across two GPU boots on GB10 (test_deepseek_v41_tilelang.py and test_deepseek_v41_ced_replay.py, 24 passed, 0 PDL violations).

Upstream-status: local candidate, prepared for upstream submission.
